# Folder Structure

Reference: `docs/FOLDER_STRUCTURE.md`

## Ownership

| Location | Owns |
|----------|------|
| `app/` | Routes, layouts, metadata, page assembly |
| `features/` | Feature UI, hooks, types, validators, views |
| `components/` | Shared, business-agnostic UI |
| `convex/` | Schema, queries, mutations, actions, auth |
| `lib/` | Shared non-React utilities |
| `hooks/` | Shared generic React hooks |
| `types/` | Shared TypeScript types |
| `services/` | External integrations (print, email, export) |
| `providers/` | App-wide providers only |
| `constants/` | Immutable shared constants |
| `styles/` | Global styles / tokens |
| `docs/` | Project documentation |
| `.cursor/` | AI rules — reference docs, do not duplicate them wholesale |

## Placement

- Feature-specific code stays in `features/<feature>/`.
- Shared UI stays in `components/`. Shared utils stay in `lib/`.
- Business rules stay in `convex/`.
- Do not create `misc`, `temp`, `new`, `old`, or similarly vague folders.

## When adding a top-level folder

Document purpose, allowed contents, and prohibited contents in `docs/FOLDER_STRUCTURE.md` in the same change.
